# Optional overrides. Copy this file to `.env` and uncomment what you need.

# The typed endpoint: Jev (TypeSafe System One) over TypeSafe's own API. It is not
# OpenAI-compatible, and its answers are typed rather than written. 302.AI proxies the same path -
# worth knowing when a key is scoped to one or the other.
# SKILLS_PROFILES_API_KEY=sk-...
# SKILLS_PROFILES_BASE_URL=https://api.typesafe.ai/v1/systemone
# SKILLS_PROFILES_MODEL=jev-latest

# Seconds per request, and the retries after one. The endpoint is fast, and drops the first call
# after it has been idle - which arrives as a timeout and is what the retries are for. With
# translation thinking on (below), a call reasons before it answers, so raise the timeout for that
# batch (120 is comfortable):
# SKILLS_PROFILES_TIMEOUT=20
# SKILLS_PROFILES_MAX_RETRIES=3

# The second endpoint: an OpenAI-compatible chat completions API translate.py asks for the Chinese
# version of each skill's one-line description. Defaults point at Xunfei Xingchen MaaS serving
# Spark-X2.5-4B; the model id is the one the console's service page (服务管控) shows, so override it
# when the subscription spells it differently. TIMEOUT and MAX_RETRIES above are shared.
# SKILLS_PROFILES_TRANSLATE_API_KEY=sk-...
# SKILLS_PROFILES_TRANSLATE_BASE_URL=https://maas-api.cn-huabei-1.xf-yun.com/v2
# SKILLS_PROFILES_TRANSLATE_MODEL=spark-x2.5-4b
# Deep thinking is on by default: the request carries the MaaS extension enable_thinking=true and
# max_tokens=32768 (the documented ceiling; its own 2048 default would cut the reasoning off). The
# reasoning arrives in `reasoning_content` and is not read - the translation is `content`.
# SKILLS_PROFILES_TRANSLATE_ENABLE_THINKING=true
# SKILLS_PROFILES_TRANSLATE_MAX_TOKENS=32768

# The second chance: a skill the chat endpoint above fails is retried once on this fallback
# endpoint, another OpenAI-compatible chat model behind the same request shape (only the model
# is swapped). It shares TIMEOUT, MAX_RETRIES and the token budget with the primary. The base
# url and model default to Agnes AI; the key is said here rather than borrowed from the typed
# endpoint's, so the two can change apart. An unset key means no fallback: a failed skill
# fails as before.
# SKILLS_PROFILES_TRANSLATE_FALLBACK_API_KEY=sk-...
# SKILLS_PROFILES_TRANSLATE_FALLBACK_BASE_URL=https://apihub.agnes-ai.com/v1
# SKILLS_PROFILES_TRANSLATE_FALLBACK_MODEL=agnes-3.0-flash

# Fake endpoint, real layout: the same thing `just dry=1` sets. No API calls, no key needed.
# SKILLS_PROFILES_DRY_RUN=1

# Everything this file can set is the scripts' own: the two endpoints, their keys and models, and
# the dry-run switch. The paths and the batch knobs are `just` variables instead -
# `just output_dir=/tmp/x`, `just limit=20 jobs=8` - so nothing here can silently change
# where a batch reads or writes.
